window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d4453a2a56aa896a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"refactor-swiftui-screens\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"swiftui\">重构 SwiftUI 页面</h1> <p>使用 Codex 将过大的 SwiftUI 页面拆分为小型子视图，同时不改变行为或布局。</p> <p>使用 Codex 和 Build iOS Apps 插件，将冗长的 SwiftUI 视图拆分为专用的分区视图，把副作用移出 <code>body</code>，稳定状态与 Observation 的用法，并优先采用 MV 思路，避免引入不必要的视图模型。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li><code>body</code> 把布局、分支逻辑、异步工作和内联操作混在一起，难以审查的大型 SwiftUI 文件。</li> <li>希望内部结构更易维护，但视觉和行为必须保持一致的现有 iOS 功能。</li> <li>使用计算得到的 <code>some View</code> 片段、可选视图模型或状态传递较复杂，且需要简化为明确子视图输入和回调的页面。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用 SwiftUI 视图重构技能提取专用子视图、保留稳定的数据流、简化 Observation 的用法，并在 Codex 修改大型 SwiftUI 页面时保持行为不变。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>UI 架构</td> <td>SwiftUI，以 <code>@State</code>、<code>@Environment</code> 和小型专用 <code>View</code> 类型为基础，优先采用 MV 思路拆分</td> <td>Codex 先简化视图树和状态流，通常比先增加一层视图模型更容易维护大型页面。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>重构工作流</td> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></td> <td>插件的 SwiftUI 视图重构技能提供了明确的提取、Observation 和副作用清理规则，同时保留原有行为。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>验证</td> <td><code>xcodebuild</code>、预览和有针对性的 UI 检查</td> <td>每次提取子视图后运行小型构建或模拟器检查，比一次性彻底重写更容易确认行为保持不变。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>重构一个大型页面，同时不改变行为</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 Build iOS Apps 插件及其 SwiftUI 视图重构技能，整理 [NameOfScreen.swift]，但不要改变页面的功能或外观。\n\n约束：\n- 除非发现必须单独指出的缺陷，否则保留行为、布局、导航和业务逻辑。\n- 默认优先采用 MV，而不是 MVVM。引入新的视图模型前，先考虑 `@State`、`@Environment`、`@Query`、`.task`、`.task(id:)` 和 `onChange`；只有功能确实需要时，才保留视图模型。\n- 重新整理视图文件，使存储属性、计算状态、`init`、`body`、视图辅助项和辅助方法从上到下都容易浏览。\n- 将有实际意义的分区提取为专用 `View` 类型，并为它们设置少量、明确的输入、`@Binding` 和回调。不要把一个超长的 `body` 改写成一堆很大的计算属性 `some View`。\n- 把复杂的按钮操作和副作用移出 `body`，放到小型方法中；把真正的业务逻辑移到服务或模型中。\n- 保持根视图树稳定。如果局部条件分区或修饰符就足够，不要使用顶层 `if/else` 来切换完全不同的页面。\n- 重构时修正 Observation 的所有权：在 iOS 17 及以上版本中，用 `@State` 保存根级 `@Observable` 模型；除非 UI 确实需要这种状态形态，否则避免使用可选或延迟初始化的视图模型。\n- 每次提取子视图后，运行能够证明页面行为保持不变的最小构建或测试检查。\n\n交付内容：\n- 重构后的页面及提取出来的子视图\n- 对新的子视图边界和数据流的简短说明\n- 有意保留视图模型的地方及原因\n- 用于证明行为保持不变的验证检查\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"refactor-one-screen-without-changing-what-it-does\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">重构一个页面，同时不改变它的功能</h2> <p>当一个 SwiftUI 文件已经长成一个庞大的页面，以至于每次小改动都让人担心时，就适合使用这个用例。目标不是重新设计功能或另造架构。请让 Codex 保留现有行为和布局，再把页面拆分为较小的子视图，并明确数据流，让下一次改动更容易审查。</p> <p>进行这类整理时，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>。它的 SwiftUI 视图重构技能有一套明确的做法：优先考虑 MV，而不是 MVVM；将业务逻辑保留在服务或模型中；先使用局部视图状态和环境依赖；只有功能明显需要时，才保留视图模型。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-ask-codex-to-do\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">告诉 Codex 要做什么</h2> <p>先指定一个具体页面文件，并要求 Codex 在改善结构的同时保留行为。可以把以下重构规则直接写进提示词：</p> <ul> <li>重新整理文件，使环境依赖、存储属性、计算得到的非视图状态、<code>init</code>、<code>body</code>、视图辅助项和辅助方法从上到下都容易浏览。</li> <li>将有实际意义的分区提取为专用 <code>View</code> 类型，并为它们设置少量、明确的输入、<code>@Binding</code> 和回调。</li> <li>少用计算属性 <code>some View</code> 辅助项，并让它们保持简短。不要把一个庞大的页面重写为一长串私有的计算视图片段。</li> <li>把复杂的按钮操作和副作用移出 <code>body</code>，并将真正的业务逻辑移到服务或模型中。</li> <li>保持根视图树稳定。优先在分区或修饰符中使用局部条件，而不是通过顶层 <code>if/else</code> 切换整个页面。</li> <li>随重构一起修正 Observation 的所有权。对于根级 <code>@Observable</code> 模型，在 iOS 17 及以上版本中，应由拥有它的视图将其保存在 <code>@State</code> 中；只有部署目标要求时，才使用旧式的可观察属性包装器。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"ask-for-a-small-validation-loop\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">采用小步验证流程</h2> <p>保留行为的重构应该有证据支持。请让 Codex 在每次重要的提取后，运行能够覆盖该页面的最小构建、预览、测试或模拟器检查，再总结结构发生了什么变化，以及哪些内容有意保持不变。</p> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">实用技巧</h2> <p><a id=\"split-first-then-debate-architecture\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">先拆分，再讨论架构</h3> <p>如果页面太大，先让 Codex 提取各个分区视图，再考虑是否需要新抽象层。更短、更明确的视图树往往能减少引入视图模型的必要。</p> <p><a id=\"pass-the-smallest-possible-interface-into-each-subview\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">只向子视图传入最精简的接口</h3> <p>优先使用 <code>let</code> 值、<code>@Binding</code> 和职责单一的回调，而不是把整个父级模型都传给每个子视图。这样，每个提取出来的分区更容易单独预览，也不容易意外地与整个父页面耦合。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-codex-to-call-out-intentional-non-changes\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex_1\">让 Codex 明确说明哪些内容有意未改</h3> <p>安全的重构应明确列出没有改动的内容，例如业务规则、导航行为、持久化、分析事件语义和用户可见布局。这样能大幅加快审查。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"refactor-swiftui-screens\">Refactor SwiftUI screens</h1> <p>Use Codex to split an oversized SwiftUI screen into small subviews without changing behavior or layout.</p> <p>Use Codex and the Build iOS Apps plugin to break a long SwiftUI view into dedicated section views, move side effects out of <code>body</code>, stabilize state and Observation usage, and keep the refactor MV-first instead of introducing unnecessary view models.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Giant SwiftUI files where <code>body</code> mixes layout, branching, async work, and inline actions in one hard-to-review screen</li> <li>Existing iOS features that should stay visually and behaviorally identical while the internals become easier to maintain</li> <li>Screens with computed <code>some View</code> fragments, optional view models, or state plumbing that should be simplified into explicit subview inputs and callbacks</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Use the SwiftUI view refactor skill to extract dedicated subviews, preserve stable data flow, simplify Observation usage, and keep behavior intact while Codex edits large SwiftUI screens.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>UI architecture</td> <td>SwiftUI with an MV-first split across <code>@State</code>, <code>@Environment</code>, and small dedicated <code>View</code> types</td> <td>Large screens usually get easier to maintain when Codex simplifies the view tree and state flow before introducing another view model layer.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Refactor workflow</td> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a></td> <td>The plugin's SwiftUI view refactor skill gives Codex clear rules for extraction, Observation, and side-effect cleanup while preserving behavior.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Validation</td> <td><code>xcodebuild</code>, previews, and focused UI checks</td> <td>Small build or simulator checks after each extraction make it easier to trust a behavior-preserving refactor than a one-shot rewrite.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Refactor One Large Screen Without Changing Behavior</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build iOS Apps plugin and its SwiftUI view refactor skill to clean up [NameOfScreen.swift] without changing what the screen does or how it looks.\n\nConstraints:\n- Preserve behavior, layout, navigation, and business logic unless you find a bug that must be called out separately.\n- Default to MV, not MVVM. Prefer `@State`, `@Environment`, `@Query`, `.task`, `.task(id:)`, and `onChange` before introducing a new view model, and only keep a view model if this feature clearly needs one.\n- Reorder the view so stored properties, computed state, `init`, `body`, view helpers, and helper methods are easy to scan top to bottom.\n- Extract meaningful sections into dedicated `View` types with small explicit inputs, `@Binding`s, and callbacks. Do not replace one giant `body` with a pile of large computed `some View` properties.\n- Move non-trivial button actions and side effects out of `body` into small methods, and move real business logic into services or models.\n- Keep the root view tree stable. Avoid top-level `if/else` branches that swap entirely different screens when localized conditional sections or modifiers are enough.\n- Fix Observation ownership while refactoring: use `@State` for root `@Observable` models on iOS 17+, and avoid optional or delayed-initialized view models unless the UI genuinely needs that state shape.\n- After each extraction, run the smallest useful build or test check that proves the screen still behaves the same.\n\nDeliver:\n- the refactored screen and any extracted subviews\n- a short explanation of the new subview boundaries and data flow\n- any places where you intentionally kept a view model and why\n- the validation checks you ran to prove behavior stayed intact\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"refactor-one-screen-without-changing-what-it-does\">Refactor one screen without changing what it does</h2> <p>This use case is for the moment when a SwiftUI file has grown into one giant screen and every small edit feels risky. The goal is not to redesign the feature or invent a new architecture. Ask Codex to preserve behavior and layout, then split the screen into small subviews with explicit data flow so the next change becomes easier to review.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a> for this kind of cleanup. Its SwiftUI view refactor skill is opinionated in a useful way: default to MV over MVVM, keep business logic in services or models, use local view state and environment dependencies first, and only keep a view model when the feature clearly needs one.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-ask-codex-to-do\">What to ask Codex to do</h2> <p>Start by naming one concrete screen file and asking Codex to preserve behavior while improving structure. These are the refactor rules worth putting directly in your prompt:</p> <ul> <li>Reorder the file so environment dependencies, stored properties, computed non-view state, <code>init</code>, <code>body</code>, view helpers, and helper methods are easy to scan top to bottom.</li> <li>Extract meaningful sections into dedicated <code>View</code> types with small explicit inputs, <code>@Binding</code>s, and callbacks.</li> <li>Keep computed <code>some View</code> helpers rare and small. Do not rebuild one giant screen as a long list of private computed view fragments.</li> <li>Move non-trivial button actions and side effects out of <code>body</code>, and move real business logic into services or models.</li> <li>Keep the root view tree stable. Prefer localized conditionals in sections or modifiers over top-level <code>if/else</code> branches that swap whole screens.</li> <li>Fix Observation ownership as you go. For root <code>@Observable</code> models on iOS 17+, the owning view should store them in <code>@State</code>; use legacy observable wrappers only when your deployment target requires that.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"ask-for-a-small-validation-loop\">Ask for a small validation loop</h2> <p>Behavior-preserving refactors should come with proof. Ask Codex to run the smallest build, preview, test, or simulator check that exercises the screen after each meaningful extraction, then summarize what changed structurally and what stayed intentionally the same.</p> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"split-first-then-debate-architecture\">Split first, then debate architecture</h3> <p>If a screen is too large, ask Codex to extract section views before introducing a new abstraction layer. A shorter, more explicit view tree often removes the pressure to add a view model at all.</p> <h3 id=\"pass-the-smallest-possible-interface-into-each-subview\">Pass the smallest possible interface into each subview</h3> <p>Prefer <code>let</code> values, <code>@Binding</code>s, and one-purpose callbacks over handing every child view the entire parent model. That makes each extracted section easier to preview and harder to accidentally couple back to the whole screen.</p> <h3 id=\"ask-codex-to-call-out-intentional-non-changes\">Ask Codex to call out intentional non-changes</h3> <p>For a safe refactor, it helps when Codex explicitly lists what it did not change: business rules, navigation behavior, persistence, analytics semantics, and user-visible layout. That makes review much faster.</p>"};
